The tree was committed unmodified first (git history: "vendor: OpenRSP 3.15.2-20 source, unmodified"),
so `git diff <that commit> -- vendor/openrsp` shows every change below exactly.

Changes made for VibeSDR (GPLv3 section 5a notice). Each is marked "VibeSDR change (2026-10-21)" in the
file, and each leaves upstream behaviour unchanged unless the option is set:

1. cmake/Platform.cmake — SDRPLAY_LINUX_UDEV (default ON). OFF builds the Linux service without
   libudev. Only the hotplug monitor uses libudev and nothing in the service calls it.
2. cmake/Platform.cmake — SDRPLAY_LIBUSB_LIBRARY / SDRPLAY_LIBUSB_INCLUDE_DIR name libusb explicitly
   instead of asking pkg-config (VibeServer links its own static libusb 1.0.30, built without udev). On
   macOS that interface also adds the IOKit, CoreFoundation and Security frameworks a static libusb needs.
3. CMakeLists.txt — SDRPLAY_STATIC_CXX_RUNTIME (default OFF). ON links libstdc++/libgcc statically
   into libsdrplay_api.so.3.15 and sdrplay_apiService, so the package depends on nothing but glibc.

4. VibeSDR change (2026-11-18) — EVERY DEVICE GETS A NAME OF ITS OWN. This one DOES change behaviour, for
   devices upstream could not handle at all. The device table, SelectDevice and the unplug check key on the
   serial, so two RSP clones reporting the same placeholder serial ("0000000001") merged into one slot (only one
   could be listed or opened), and a device with no serial string (iSerialNumber 0 — an original RSP1, many
   clones) failed the whole scan, hiding every RSP on the machine.
   - src/service/Enumerator.cpp — scanDevicesLocked(): a device with no serial string is listed with an empty
     serial instead of failing the scan; uniqueNames() then names every scanned device apart: a device the table
     already holds (same bus identity) keeps its name, so a radio on air is never renamed; otherwise, in USB port
     order, the first of a serial keeps it and each repeat becomes "<serial>_<port>", and a device with no serial
     is "RSP_<port>" (<port> = "<bus>-<p>[.<p>…]"). A device with a unique serial is untouched.
   - src/service/Enumerator.h — the uniqueNames() declaration.
   - src/platform/Usb.h — UsbDeviceInfo::portPath; src/platform/common/UsbLibusb.cpp fills it from
     libusb_get_port_numbers() (empty elsewhere: the bus and port number are used instead).
   Tested by vibeserver/test-openrsp-names.cpp (scripts/test-openrsp-names.sh).

How VibeServer builds it: vibeserver/CMakeLists.txt, section "OpenRSP". docs/OPENRSP-BUNDLE-PLAN.md
gives the reasoning, and covers each platform.
